WEBVTT

00:04.680 --> 00:06.955
- Excuse me.
- Gesundheit.

00:09.360 --> 00:10.349
Sorry.

00:10.520 --> 00:12.317
I hope I'm not coming down
with something.

00:19.440 --> 00:20.873
You think you might be?

00:21.040 --> 00:24.953
Well, I've been feeling a little congested,
and I think it's settling in my chest.

00:25.640 --> 00:27.835
That's certainly
where I was planning to settle.

00:28.320 --> 00:30.390
Maybe I should go home.

00:30.560 --> 00:31.549
Let's not overreact.

00:32.160 --> 00:34.549
We can still do this.
We just have to be careful.

00:34.720 --> 00:36.039
What do you mean?

00:36.200 --> 00:37.428
Well, we can keep kissing...

00:37.600 --> 00:41.115
...but, you know, Amish-style
with the tongues parked in the barn.

00:41.760 --> 00:44.228
If you need to cough or sneeze,
tap me on the shoulder...

00:44.400 --> 00:46.391
...and I'll cover your face
with a pillow.

00:47.400 --> 00:48.958
And...

00:51.000 --> 00:52.877
- You can use this.
- Nasal spray.

00:53.040 --> 00:54.871
Thank you. That's so thoughtful.

00:55.040 --> 00:58.237
Well, you are gonna need to breathe
through your nose.

01:07.680 --> 01:09.716
- Wanna see a movie today?
- With you?

01:09.880 --> 01:12.110
- Yeah, with me.
- No, thanks.

01:14.320 --> 01:15.309
Okay.

01:15.480 --> 01:17.277
- Wanna do something else?
- Like what?

01:17.440 --> 01:19.158
I don't know. Anything.

01:19.320 --> 01:21.231
Well, can we go
to Les Girls, Girls, Girls?

01:24.760 --> 01:26.432
- What?
- That place near the airport.

01:26.600 --> 01:29.637
Looks real interesting.
I think it's French.

01:30.760 --> 01:34.355
No, no, we're not going
to Les Girls, Girls, Girls.

01:35.040 --> 01:37.554
Then don't say we can do anything.

01:37.880 --> 01:38.869
Okay, forget it.

01:40.680 --> 01:43.069
- You really wanna do something?
- Yes.

01:43.240 --> 01:46.232
How about, drive me to the mall,
so I can see a movie with friends...

01:46.400 --> 01:48.470
...and then you pick me up
when we're done?

01:48.640 --> 01:50.392
And what am I supposed to do?

01:50.760 --> 01:53.558
Well, if I were you,
I'd go to Les Girls, Girls, Girls.

01:57.080 --> 01:59.514
Who's going to Les Girls, Girls, Girls?

01:59.880 --> 02:01.916
- Nobody.
- Too bad.

02:02.080 --> 02:03.911
Daytime's better.

02:04.360 --> 02:07.318
Dancers are a little worse for wear,
but they try harder.

02:10.040 --> 02:12.634
Oh, God, I should have sent
that woman home...

02:12.800 --> 02:15.075
...as soon as I saw
the first snot bubble.

02:15.800 --> 02:17.358
I'm done.

02:18.080 --> 02:20.310
Me too. Get dressed.
I'll drive you to the mall.

02:20.480 --> 02:21.595
Cool.

02:21.760 --> 02:23.352
Will you make me soup before you go?

02:23.760 --> 02:25.637
- I don't have time, Charlie.
- But I'm sick.

02:25.800 --> 02:28.360
- Who's gonna take care of me?
- What do you want me to say?

02:28.520 --> 02:30.909
Maybe if you bothered
to develop a human relationship...

02:31.080 --> 02:33.435
...that involved more than
the thoughtless exchange...

02:33.600 --> 02:36.353
...of bodily fluids, you'd have somebody
to take care of you.

02:37.960 --> 02:41.999
The whole time you were talking,
you could have opened a can of soup.

02:51.680 --> 02:53.113
Morning.

02:53.280 --> 02:54.872
Hey, Berta.

02:56.920 --> 02:58.239
What's wrong with you?

02:58.400 --> 02:59.799
I caught something.

02:59.960 --> 03:02.076
There's a surprise.

03:02.560 --> 03:04.630
Yeah, it's really bad.

03:04.800 --> 03:09.590
Throat, sinuses, stomachaches, chills.

03:09.760 --> 03:13.275
I swear to God,
I feel like I'm gonna die.

03:16.240 --> 03:18.071
Okay.

03:18.600 --> 03:21.433
Well, good luck.

03:43.600 --> 03:44.919
This is it.

03:45.080 --> 03:46.911
I'm a goner.

03:51.800 --> 03:53.711
Hello?

03:54.160 --> 03:56.196
Anybody here?

03:57.200 --> 04:00.397
Anybody gonna take care
of good old Charlie?

04:02.160 --> 04:03.149
Okay, then.

04:04.880 --> 04:07.758
Time to scrape
the bottom of the barrel.

04:10.720 --> 04:12.756
Mommy, I don't feel good.

04:12.920 --> 04:17.471
Oh, Charles, don't tell me you've got
another case of the Bangkok drippy-drip.

04:18.000 --> 04:19.319
No offense.

04:19.480 --> 04:22.358
No, no, it's just a cold or a flu.

04:22.520 --> 04:24.158
And this concerns me how?

04:24.760 --> 04:27.957
Well, I thought maybe you could
come over and make me some soup...

04:28.120 --> 04:30.509
...or put a cool, wet cloth on my head.

04:30.680 --> 04:33.638
Oh, darling, I'd love to.

04:33.800 --> 04:37.509
&lt;i>But, unfortunately, Mommy's sick too.&lt;/i>

04:40.960 --> 04:42.712
All right, that does sound bad.

04:42.880 --> 04:44.359
Oh, it is.

04:50.680 --> 04:51.669
What was that?

04:51.840 --> 04:53.910
Oh, just my delirious fever babble.

04:54.080 --> 04:55.149
Bye, dear.

04:56.960 --> 05:00.077
All right. I'm on my own.

05:04.640 --> 05:08.235
Maybe a little fresh air and sunshine.

05:10.520 --> 05:13.239
And nighttime cold medicine.

05:15.080 --> 05:20.837
Fresh air, sunshine,
and nighttime cold medicine.

05:23.160 --> 05:24.912
And Scotch.

05:28.160 --> 05:33.109
Fresh air, sunshine,
nighttime cold medicine...

05:33.280 --> 05:35.111
...and Scotch.

05:52.440 --> 05:53.475
Okay.

05:53.640 --> 05:56.473
Just nighttime cold medicine
and Scotch.

06:08.120 --> 06:09.792
Hey, Charlie.

06:13.520 --> 06:16.193
Rose? I thought you were in England.

06:16.960 --> 06:18.996
I was asked to leave.

06:19.680 --> 06:22.831
A little misunderstanding
at Buckingham Palace.

06:23.200 --> 06:24.269
So how are you?

06:24.840 --> 06:26.717
Not too good. I'm sick.

06:30.240 --> 06:32.629
Poor baby.

06:32.800 --> 06:34.677
Isn't anybody taking care of you?

06:34.840 --> 06:36.671
No. I'm all alone.

06:36.840 --> 06:38.353
Well, that's just not right.

06:38.520 --> 06:39.635
I'll take care of you.

06:40.000 --> 06:41.752
- You will?
- Of course.

06:41.920 --> 06:43.956
Do you want me to make you
some soup?

06:44.120 --> 06:45.269
I would love soup.

06:45.440 --> 06:49.399
I asked everybody to make me soup.
You'd think I was asking for a kidney.

06:50.920 --> 06:54.549
- What are you doing?
- Nighttime cold medicine and Scotch.

06:56.480 --> 06:59.313
I call it the Drunken Hulk.

06:59.880 --> 07:01.791
No, sweetie. I have something better.

07:02.240 --> 07:03.832
I doubt it.

07:04.440 --> 07:05.793
Well, this is new.

07:05.960 --> 07:07.029
Just approved in Europe.

07:07.200 --> 07:09.077
Oh, Europe. Give me.

07:12.480 --> 07:13.913
That's my little man.

07:14.080 --> 07:15.638
Now I'll go and make you that soup.

07:16.320 --> 07:17.878
Thank you.

07:21.120 --> 07:24.271
Okay, Europe, let's see what you got.

07:25.440 --> 07:27.476
That was a great pill.

07:27.640 --> 07:30.279
What was in that pill?
That's a great pill.

07:30.680 --> 07:32.477
Don't you worry about that.

07:32.640 --> 07:33.868
You just get your rest.

07:34.880 --> 07:36.438
You know what else is great?

07:36.600 --> 07:39.319
You showed up exactly
when I needed you the most.

07:39.480 --> 07:41.596
It's like you're my guardian angel.

07:41.760 --> 07:44.513
Hey, you think I can get another one
of those pills?

07:45.040 --> 07:46.029
No, sweetie.

07:46.200 --> 07:47.553
One's enough for now.

07:47.720 --> 07:49.119
Just go to sleep.

07:49.280 --> 07:50.679
Okay.

07:50.840 --> 07:52.319
Good night.

07:52.640 --> 07:54.756
Good night, Charlie.

08:15.840 --> 08:17.432
Can you hear me?

08:21.880 --> 08:24.314
Listen closely to my voice.

08:24.480 --> 08:26.869
You're very, very sick.

08:27.040 --> 08:29.600
I'm very, very sick.

08:29.760 --> 08:30.875
But don't worry.

08:31.040 --> 08:33.600
Rose is gonna take care of you.

08:33.760 --> 08:36.354
Rose is gonna take care of me.

08:36.520 --> 08:38.715
Till death do us part.

08:42.240 --> 08:44.629
I'm gonna need another pill.

08:47.520 --> 08:50.637
Wouldn't kill you to thank me
for dropping you off and picking you up.

08:50.800 --> 08:52.950
Thank you for dropping me off
and picking me up.

08:53.120 --> 08:54.917
- Jake, Jake, wait.
- What?

08:56.400 --> 08:59.233
Okay, listen, I know
you're getting to that age where you'd...

08:59.400 --> 09:02.392
...rather be with your friends
than your old man, and that's okay.

09:02.560 --> 09:05.358
It's completely normal for you
to wanna take your first steps...

09:05.520 --> 09:07.112
...to manhood on your own.

09:07.280 --> 09:08.395
I applaud that.

09:08.560 --> 09:13.714
But I just hope that, while you're
on this path, that every now and then...

09:13.880 --> 09:16.314
...you'll make an effort
to carve out a little Dad time.

09:24.280 --> 09:25.633
Well, that was humiliating.

09:29.200 --> 09:30.713
Charlie?

09:30.920 --> 09:32.592
How are you feeling?

09:35.640 --> 09:38.074
- Rose?
- Hi, Alan.

09:39.200 --> 09:42.033
- What are you doing here?
- Taking care of Charlie.

09:42.200 --> 09:43.189
I'm very, very sick.

09:46.280 --> 09:47.838
Go for it.

09:54.600 --> 09:56.079
So how long are you back in town?

09:56.240 --> 09:57.753
As long as Charlie needs me.

09:58.120 --> 10:01.112
Well, don't let that big baby
take advantage of your good nature.

10:01.480 --> 10:03.994
Don't worry, Berta.
I'm fine taking care of him.

10:04.160 --> 10:06.799
Well, that's good,
because nobody else wants to.

10:07.680 --> 10:11.673
The truth is, I just love feeding him,
cleaning him, changing him.

10:11.840 --> 10:13.592
- You're changing him?
- Cleaning him?

10:13.760 --> 10:16.718
You know, if you stop feeding him,
you won't have to change him.

10:18.120 --> 10:20.634
I don't mind. I'm a loving nurturer.

10:20.800 --> 10:23.792
Uncle Charlie says
you're a crazy stalker.

10:25.120 --> 10:27.031
Potato, potato.

10:27.920 --> 10:30.150
Hey, Rose,
you wanna go see a movie later?

10:30.320 --> 10:32.436
Maybe. We'll see
how your uncle's feeling.

10:32.800 --> 10:35.473
He's very, very sick.

10:38.080 --> 10:40.469
So, basically,
what we're saying here is...

10:40.960 --> 10:43.679
...you'll go to the movies
with anybody but me.

10:43.840 --> 10:45.592
Not anybody.

10:46.560 --> 10:48.391
I wouldn't go with Hitler.

10:52.960 --> 10:54.154
Charlie?

10:54.320 --> 10:56.117
I'm in here.

10:56.280 --> 10:57.998
What are you doing out of bed?

10:58.360 --> 10:59.839
What do you think?

11:00.280 --> 11:02.191
Let me help you.

11:04.440 --> 11:06.158
Yeah, Rose, I got this.

11:06.320 --> 11:07.958
Just relax, sweetie.

11:08.120 --> 11:09.553
I said I got it.

11:09.720 --> 11:11.358
Let go.

11:11.520 --> 11:14.830
You're sick.
You shouldn't be lifting anything.

11:15.480 --> 11:16.993
All right. I'm done.

11:17.160 --> 11:18.752
Need a shake?

11:18.920 --> 11:19.989
No, thanks.

11:20.160 --> 11:21.309
Okey-dokey.

11:21.480 --> 11:24.199
Now let's get you back into bed.

11:25.280 --> 11:30.229
Rose, I appreciate you taking care of me,
but I'm thinking the worst is over.

11:30.400 --> 11:32.152
That's your mind playing tricks on you.

11:32.320 --> 11:34.675
If you start running around too soon,
you'll relapse.

11:34.840 --> 11:37.195
- Maybe get pneumonia.
- Pneumonia?

11:37.360 --> 11:39.271
Lungs fill up with fluid.
You can't breathe.

11:39.440 --> 11:41.715
And you end up drowning
in your own mucus.

11:42.120 --> 11:43.599
You don't want that, do you?

11:43.760 --> 11:46.399
I don't wanna drown
in anybody's mucus.

11:48.280 --> 11:49.599
Of course, you don't.

11:50.080 --> 11:51.638
Open.

11:52.960 --> 11:54.632
Good boy.

11:57.600 --> 12:00.160
I am really lucky to have you, Rose.

12:00.320 --> 12:02.356
You know what, Charlie?

12:02.720 --> 12:04.756
I think we make our own luck.

12:05.240 --> 12:07.674
- We do?
- Well...

12:08.480 --> 12:09.515
I do.

13:08.920 --> 13:10.592
Rose?

13:12.080 --> 13:13.911
Hello?

13:14.080 --> 13:16.150
Anybody there?

13:25.120 --> 13:27.190
What the hell?

13:33.840 --> 13:35.751
Oh, that's not right.

13:36.960 --> 13:38.632
Alan. Alan.

13:39.400 --> 13:41.755
Alan!

13:47.160 --> 13:48.639
What's the matter?

13:48.960 --> 13:50.916
How long have I been up here?

13:51.440 --> 13:54.671
- I don't know. About two weeks?
- Two weeks?

13:56.120 --> 13:57.599
Didn't you think to check on me?

13:57.920 --> 14:00.514
Well, frankly, everything was going
so smoothly around here.

14:00.680 --> 14:02.398
It never occurred to me.

14:03.960 --> 14:05.871
- Are those knit booties?
- What?

14:07.200 --> 14:09.919
- I don't know.
- Since when do you wear knit booties?

14:10.600 --> 14:12.591
Since when do I have
turquoise fingernails?

14:14.080 --> 14:16.469
- Where's Rose?
- She went to the movies with Jake.

14:16.640 --> 14:18.915
God forbid my son
should go anywhere with his father.

14:19.080 --> 14:21.674
- I mean, I have tried everything...
- Alan, listen to me.

14:22.840 --> 14:25.354
- You cannot let Rose back in this house.
- Why not?

14:25.520 --> 14:28.159
The cold pills she's been giving me
are not cold pills.

14:28.320 --> 14:30.151
- What do you think they are?
- I don't know.

14:30.320 --> 14:33.073
Something you give to elephants
when they can't sleep.

14:34.160 --> 14:37.835
- Elephants?
- European elephants.

14:38.560 --> 14:40.312
You know,
I think you might be delirious.

14:40.480 --> 14:42.630
- You really should lie down.
- Screw that.

14:42.800 --> 14:44.631
I'm getting out
before she comes back.

14:44.800 --> 14:47.473
Are those comfy?
Because they look really comfy.

14:47.640 --> 14:48.914
Charlie.

14:49.360 --> 14:50.349
What are you doing up?

14:51.320 --> 14:52.878
Stay away from me, Rose.

14:53.040 --> 14:55.110
- What's wrong, honey?
- Don't you call me honey.

14:55.280 --> 14:57.077
Charlie, Charlie,
you need to calm down.

14:57.240 --> 14:58.309
Calm down?

14:58.560 --> 15:01.028
Thanks to her, I've been
a drooling vegetable for weeks.

15:01.200 --> 15:03.509
I was afraid of this.
He's running a very high fever.

15:03.680 --> 15:07.434
- He's hallucinating.
- I am not running a fever. Here, feel me.

15:07.600 --> 15:08.589
I am not hot.

15:08.760 --> 15:11.194
A little clammy and none too fresh,
but not hot.

15:11.360 --> 15:13.351
Just relax, baby. You need your rest.

15:13.520 --> 15:15.909
No, no, no, what I need is a lawyer.

15:19.240 --> 15:21.674
Alan, please, you gotta believe me.
I am not sick.

15:21.840 --> 15:23.193
I believe you. Now, lay down.

15:23.360 --> 15:25.999
- But, Alan...
- It's for your own good.

15:32.160 --> 15:33.513
Okay. Okay, you're right.

15:33.680 --> 15:35.511
I'm crazy from the fever.

15:35.680 --> 15:37.352
Not crazy, honey.

15:37.520 --> 15:40.080
Just very, very sick.

15:40.880 --> 15:42.552
Now, open up.

15:43.320 --> 15:45.675
Good boy. Swallow.

15:46.520 --> 15:49.910
There you go. Now, get some rest.

15:52.640 --> 15:56.394
So does a guy have to be sick
to get a pair of those booties?

16:07.280 --> 16:10.829
Thank God
she wasn't using suppositories.

16:32.280 --> 16:34.714
Son of a bitch.

16:34.880 --> 16:36.791
Charlie, are you up?

17:13.120 --> 17:14.519
Alan.

17:18.160 --> 17:20.799
- What are you doing?
- Escaping.

17:21.120 --> 17:22.519
Charlie, this isn't a good time.

17:22.680 --> 17:24.477
I've already had
my second cup of coffee.

17:24.880 --> 17:26.871
Look, I don't know how long I've got.

17:27.040 --> 17:28.632
Neither do I.

17:31.520 --> 17:33.511
Oh, damn it. She's out.

17:34.320 --> 17:37.232
- Out of what?
- Her freaking mind.

17:37.680 --> 17:39.591
Charlie, where are you?

17:40.040 --> 17:42.076
Oh, God, she's coming.
Is your door locked?

17:42.240 --> 17:43.559
No. Neither was my window.

17:43.720 --> 17:45.551
Two mistakes I will never make again.

17:46.360 --> 17:48.590
Charlie, are you in here?

17:49.320 --> 17:51.675
- Rose.
- Sorry, Alan. Have you seen Charlie?

17:51.840 --> 17:53.512
Bathtub.

17:58.240 --> 18:00.310
For God's sake, Alan,
you're my brother.

18:02.320 --> 18:05.756
Oh, Charlie, is this how you act
after everything I've done for you?

18:06.200 --> 18:07.838
Yes. This is how I act.

18:08.000 --> 18:10.150
Playing Anne Frank in the bathtub.

18:10.640 --> 18:13.473
Well, I give up. I can't take care of you
if you won't cooperate.

18:13.920 --> 18:16.195
Oh, no, no, Rose. Let's not be hasty.

18:16.360 --> 18:18.715
It's been so nice
these last couple of weeks.

18:18.880 --> 18:20.757
What if Charlie promises
to behave himself?

18:20.920 --> 18:23.354
I am not promising
Nurse Ratched anything.

18:24.160 --> 18:25.718
Well, then I guess I'll just leave.

18:27.720 --> 18:29.312
- You're not leaving.
- I was bluffing.

18:29.480 --> 18:30.799
- Rose.
- Darn.

18:33.920 --> 18:36.912
I hope you are proud of yourself.
All she was trying to do was help.

18:37.080 --> 18:40.390
No, no, no,
that's not what she was trying to do.

18:41.440 --> 18:43.476
This was all a plot.

18:43.640 --> 18:45.039
It started with getting me sick.

18:45.200 --> 18:47.714
She drugged me to keep me helpless
so she could move in...

18:47.880 --> 18:50.952
...and have her way with me.
- Oh, really? Rose got you sick.

18:51.120 --> 18:54.999
Nothing to do with sticking your tongue
down the throat of a flu-riddled bimbo?

18:55.520 --> 18:57.829
I'm not saying I know how she did it,
but she did it.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.150
Any idea how insane
this makes you sound?

19:00.320 --> 19:03.118
I have proof. Come on, I'll show you.

19:03.960 --> 19:05.359
Charlie?

19:07.600 --> 19:09.352
Fine. I'll wait outside.

19:15.280 --> 19:16.872
I'm bored. Wanna go see a movie?

19:17.360 --> 19:19.749
- Now?
- Well, you got the listings there.

19:19.920 --> 19:21.717
Jake, for the love of God.

19:21.880 --> 19:23.598
Fine. But don't say I never ask.

19:27.960 --> 19:29.916
You'll see. I have proof.

19:30.080 --> 19:32.640
I didn't swallow the last pill,
so we can have it analyzed.

19:33.080 --> 19:36.755
Right. I'll call CSI
and have them run some tests.

19:38.720 --> 19:40.472
I hid it under my pillow and...

19:46.240 --> 19:48.993
Okay, I don't have proof.

19:57.520 --> 19:58.509
Rose?

19:58.920 --> 20:00.319
Oh, hi, Lulu.

20:00.880 --> 20:03.110
- How'd your plan work out?
- Well, you were fine.

20:03.280 --> 20:05.919
But I think I may have overplayed it.

20:06.080 --> 20:08.958
If you wanna take another swing at him,
I'm coming down with mono.

20:09.120 --> 20:11.509
Oh, Charlie's already had mono.

20:11.680 --> 20:13.910
Give me a call if you get mumps
or whooping cough.

20:14.080 --> 20:15.433
Will do.

20:25.840 --> 20:28.149
Oh, Rose.

20:39.200 --> 20:42.431
Oh, God, not another one.

21:06.440 --> 21:08.431
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:08.600 --> 21:10.591
[ENGLISH]
